1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
GRINDING BRAKES -- but only the FIRST stop of the day?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
If your car sat overnight -- or in the rain -- this can point to
something on the rotor, not the pads

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A thin layer of surface rust can form on the rotor face.
It's one clue, not a verdict

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
It usually wipes off within the first few stops of the drive

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Still grinding after that? Worth checking.
Do not guess -- stop by and we'll take a look

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
SAVE THIS | DM "BRAKES"
